<title>UK: Newman Tonks leaps on FKI approach.</title>
<headline>Newman Tonks leaps on FKI approach.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Newman Tonks Plc jumped in early trading on Monday after the architecural ironmongery supplier said it had received an approach from engineering group FKI that might lead to a bid.</p>
<p>The stock was up 26-1/2p at 129 by 0832 GMT while FKI was down 1p at 200-1/2.  </p>
<p>In a brief statement Newman Tonks said that it had received an approach from FKI &quot;which may or may not lead to an offer being made for the company.&quot;</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
</text>
